  CVE-2026-7737|2026-05-04T07:16:01.700|2026-05-05T19:12:45.533|6.9|MEDIUM|CWE-119|N/A|false|A vulnerability was identified in osrg GoBGP up to 4.3.0. Affected by this issue is the function BMPPeerUpNotification.ParseBody/BMPStatisticsReport.ParseBody of the file pkg/packet/bmp/bmp.go of the component BMP Parser. The manipulation leads to out-of-bounds read. The attack can be initiated remotely. Upgrading to version 4.4.0 can resolve this issue. The identifier of the patch is bc77597d42335c78464bc8e15a471d887bbdf260. Upgrading the affected component is recommended.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-7737|0.00047|0.14084|4.8314
