  CVE-2026-37457|2026-05-01T18:16:14.770|2026-05-01T19:16:30.247|7.5|HIGH|CWE-787|N/A|false|An off-by-one out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the bgp_flowspec_op_decode() function (bgpd/bgp_flowspec_util.c) of FRRouting (FRR) stable/10.0 allows attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) via supplying a crafted FlowSpec component.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-37457|0.00040|0.11838|5.2512
  CVE-2026-35233|2026-05-01T18:16:14.647|2026-05-05T17:46:30.743|4.4|MEDIUM|CWE-125|N/A|false|An unprivileged attacker can craft a user-space process with a malicious ELF binary containing an out-of-range sh_link field. When root-level dtrace attaches to -- or instruments -- that process (via dtrace -p , pid probes, or USDT), the ELF parser reads heap memory beyond the allocated section cache array without any bounds check. This results in an uninitialized/out-of-bounds heap read that can cause a NULL pointer dereference crash of the dtrace process (DoS), or -- depending on heap layout -- a read-then-use of a garbage pointer controlled by adjacent allocations, providing a foothold toward further exploitation in a privileged context.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35233|0.00013|0.02165|3.0804
  CVE-2026-26461|2026-05-01T18:16:14.307|2026-05-01T19:16:29.643|6.5|MEDIUM|CWE-77|N/A|false|A Command Injection vulnerability in the web management interface in Aver PTC320UV2 0.1.0000.65 allows an unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary commands via a crafted web request.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26461|0.06746|0.91336|4.7524
