  CVE-2025-69606|2026-05-01T18:16:13.607|2026-05-01T19:16:29.350|6.1|MEDIUM|CWE-79|N/A|false|Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability was discovered in the GSVoIP web panel version 2.0.90. The `msg` parameter in the `/painel/gateways.php/error` endpoint does not properly sanitize user-supplied input, allowing attackers to inject arbitrary JavaScript into the HTML response. A remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted URL to a victim, leading to unauthorized script execution, session hijacking, phishing, or other client-side attacks.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-69606|0.00045|0.13545|4.2713
